 "about": "Every AI model Hearth OS offers for Colibri (Server mode › AI engine), in two groups. \"standard\" is Colibri's own catalog (Hearth reads it live from `coli setup --list --all --json`; this is the v2.1.0 copy for apps that only read files). \"uncensored\" are abliterated GGUF builds on Hugging Face of models Colibri runs (architectures qwen3moe and qwen35moe, docs/gguf.md), each confirmed to exist; Hearth downloads one over https with resume, checks its size and its SHA-256 as Hugging Face publishes it, then runs `coli import`. Sizes are bytes as Hugging Face lists them; the RAM figures for the GGUF builds are Hearth's estimate (Colibri's planner decides on the real files).",
